    key_claims:['Yuanshi Tianzun: Celestial Worthy of Original Beginning — first of the Three','Lingbao Tianzun: Celestial Worthy of Numinous Treasure — second, keeper of scriptures','Daode Tianzun: Celestial Worthy of the Way and Its Power — Laozi deified','The Three Pure Ones rule the Three Heavens and are the highest personal expressions of the Tao','They preexist creation and will continue after the cosmos dissolves'],
    essence:'The Three Pure Ones are the Tao\'s first and highest personal manifestations — the divine council of Taoism. The Tao itself cannot be worshipped (it is beyond relation), but the Three Pure Ones can be approached, and they govern the celestial realm. Daode Tianzun is Laozi himself elevated to cosmic divinity — the sage who descended to teach humanity.',
