    primary_sources:['Kalachakra Tantra','Guhyasamaja Tantra','Vajrayana canonical texts'],
    key_claims:['Adi-Buddha is the primordial, self-created Buddha — the source from which all other Buddhas emanate','The Trikaya (three-body doctrine): Dharmakaya (truth-body) = Tier 1; Sambhogakaya (bliss-body) = Tier 2; Nirmanakaya (emanation-body) = Cross-Tier','Vajradhara is the Adi-Buddha in Tibetan Vajrayana — holding the vajra (thunderbolt of enlightenment)','Five Dhyani Buddhas emanate from Adi-Buddha as cosmic presences','In Theravada: this framework is considered later development; in Vajrayana: it is the central cosmology'],
    essence:'The Adi-Buddha sits at the apex of the Vajrayana cosmic hierarchy — the primordial, self-originated awareness from which all manifestations of enlightenment flow. The five Dhyani Buddhas are not separate beings but aspects of the one primordial enlightened mind radiating in five directions. The Trikaya translates this into three levels: the formless truth-body (approaching Tier 1), the divine form-body accessible to advanced practitioners (Tier 2), and the historical teachers who appear in the world (Cross-Tier).',
    parallel_node_ids:['barbelo-aeons','el-elyon','three-pure-ones'],
