    key_claims:['The Aesir under Odin form the divine council that governs the nine worlds','Odin, Thor, Freya (Vanir adopted), Tyr, Baldr, Loki (adopted), Heimdall — the inner council','The Aesir are not eternal — they will die at Ragnarok; this is a unique feature of Norse cosmology','They meet at Urdarbrunnr (the Well of Fate) at the base of Yggdrasil to deliberate','The norns (fate-weavers) even govern the Aesir — they too are subject to fate'],
    essence:'The Aesir are the Tier 2 council of Norse cosmology — but with a profound difference from all other Tier 2 councils: they know they will die. Odin knows he will be swallowed by Fenrir at Ragnarok. Thor knows he will kill and be killed by the Midgard Serpent. They govern despite knowing their governance is temporary. This is the Norse theological statement about the nature of the divine: even the highest council is not ultimate.',
