    key_claims:['In Prometheus Bound: Zeus is the tyrant who tortures Prometheus for giving fire to humanity','Zeus overthrew his own father Kronos — yet chains Prometheus for the same liberating impulse','Even Zeus is subject to the Fates (Moirai) — he is not the highest principle','"God of THIS world" in his binding aspect — enforcer of limitation','The same Zeus who chains Prometheus has a council aspect (Tier 2) — his Tier 3 role is specific'],
    essence:'Zeus in his tyrant aspect is the power that punishes liberation. He chains Prometheus to the rock for giving fire (consciousness, technology, self-awareness) to humanity. He is the enforcer of limitation — the cosmic power who says "they were not supposed to have that." He is the god of this world in its binding mode.',
