    key_claims:['Mara attacked the Buddha under the Bodhi Tree with armies of desire, aversion, and ignorance','Rules the Kamadhatu — the realm of sensory desire, lowest of the three realms','Appears throughout the Pali Canon trying to tempt and distract the Buddha and his disciples','Mara is not a cosmic dualist enemy but the forces that keep beings trapped in samsara','The Buddha\'s response: "I see you, Mara" — recognition dissolves his power'],
    essence:'Mara is the Buddhist ruler of the realm of desire — and the force who attacked the Buddha at the moment of his awakening. His armies are desire, aversion, and ignorance: the three poisons that keep beings trapped in samsara. The Buddha\'s response to Mara\'s attack was recognition: "I see you, Mara." Not war, not suppression — recognition. Mara\'s power depends on not being seen for what he is.',
