    key_claims:['The Qliphoth are the anti-Sefirot — the shadow structure on the inverse Tree of Life','Each Sefirah has a corresponding Qliphah — a distorted, limited reflection','The Sitra Achra (Other Side) is the realm of demonic forces in Kabbalistic theology','The Qliphoth came into being from the shevirat ha-kelim — the shattering of the vessels of divine light','Tikkun (repair) is partly the work of elevating the divine sparks trapped in the Qliphotic shells'],
    essence:'The Qliphoth are the husks — the shells left over when divine light withdrew from broken vessels. They are not independently evil in origin but the accumulation of limitation, distortion, and the aftermath of cosmic breakage. Each of the ten Sefirot has a Qliphotic shadow — a perversion of its proper function. The Talmudic warning: "Do not investigate the Qliphoth" is itself evidence of how seriously the tradition takes this domain.',
