    key_claims:['Seven Archons, one per classical planet: Moon, Mercury, Venus, Sun, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn','Named: Ialtabaoth, Iao, Sabaoth, Adonaios, Astaphaios, Ailoaios, Horaios','Their seven heavens form the barrier the ascending soul must pass through','Each Archon governs a specific aspect of fate and limitation in the material world','The soul ascending after death must know the passwords (gnosis) to pass through each Archon'],
    essence:'The seven Archons are Yaldabaoth\'s children and lieutenants — each governing one of the seven classical planets that, in ancient cosmology, determined human fate. To be born is to descend through their seven spheres. To ascend after death is to shed their qualities sphere by sphere, presenting the correct formula (gnosis) at each gate. They are not evil in the simple sense — they are the administrators of the material order, doing exactly what they were made to do.',
