    key_claims:['200 Watchers descended on Mount Hermon and swore an oath to each other','Taught humanity: metallurgy, weaponry, astrology, cosmetics, enchantments, root-cutting','Azazel the Watcher: "taught men to make swords and knives" — bound in the desert until Judgment','Daniel 10: the prince of Persia and the prince of Greece — angelic powers governing nations','Deuteronomy 32 (DSS): the nations were distributed among the "sons of God" — these are the Watchers'],
    essence:'The Watchers are the sons of God who descended. Two hundred of them descended on Mount Hermon, swore an oath, and took human wives. Their children were the Nephilim. They taught humanity forbidden arts — and for this they were bound. But from a different angle: they are the angelic powers assigned to govern the nations (Daniel 10), some of whom crossed the boundary, and some of whom became Cross-Tier liberators in doing so.',
